-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved

  Replay      cauldron.rzx (89,596 frames, Dean's recording of this release)
              IDENTICAL on rework v11 round 2: 84,638 plots (42,188 draws,
              41,855 erases), PR-ALL 53,334, tile 28,399, scrolls 1,760 /
              3,552, clears 110, CL-LINE 64; 268.7M sprite pixels; the sprite
              model with pending hides (an erase's sprite stays until the
              commit of the draw that replaces it) at every event and every
              body start; every commit checked against a model beam; attribute
              shadow + ULA model, no unhooked attribute access; 105 unit cases
              PASS, 24 negative controls detected (new: the hide at the
              erase's end, the build before round 2; a commit without the beam
              wait); clock matrix 17 hook sites x 4 incoming clocks = 68
              cases, exit = the incoming speed, a forced 3.5 MHz exit
              detected; ROM paths pass (known: the 4 ROM-site JPs); start-up
              tail never read before written. CL-SCROLL never reached

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: loading screen, menu, play reached,
              frames viewed; flicker 900 frames (600-1499) against the
              original: 0 one-frame picture transients, 0 vanished figures, 0
              out of step, 1.20 picture changes a game update (the original
              1.72); before round 2 the same frames had 23 transients, each on
              a gap between an erase's hide and the next draw's show crossed
              by the beam; 15-minute soak against the original: no freeze,
              loop or crash; no person played it

  Coverage    loading screen stub in bank 22, emulator-tested only (the replay
              is of the build without it); cheats proved in the simulator on
              the original (Kempston random play, 12,000 frames): Infinite
              lives: lives 8 held (without: 8 to 3); Infinite magic: magic
              held at 99 (without: 99 to 0); Infinite Hags dropped (the same
              counter as the lives), Finish game dropped (no effect: the game
              resets 41289), the value-asking entries not importable

  Hardware    none (Dean ran v1.0 43c1ca49 on a Next, 2026-10-27; v1.1
              untested)

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
